WEBVTT

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.300
Welcome back, I'm awful glad to see you today.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.620
Today, let's do something that's bright and shiny

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.840
that'll put you in a good mood

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.800
and do nice things in your heart here.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.180
So I'm gonna have them graphically run all the colors

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.700
across the screen that we'll use to do the painting today.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:45.320
And they'll come across your screen in the same order

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.460
that I have them on my palette,

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.600
starting with a white and coming around.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.920
And while they're doing that, let's get started.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.340
I've already covered the canvas

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.000
with a thin, even coat of Magic White,

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.000
and we're ready to go.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.760
Today, I'm gonna start with a little tiny bit

00:00:58.760 --> 00:00:59.580
of Indian yellow.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.460
and we'll just put a little bit on our 2 1⁄2 inch brush.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:07.210
Okay, now let's go right up here in the sky,

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.560
and we'll start making little X's, little tiny X's.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.780
You don't need much color.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.160
Blends with a magic white,

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:21.790
and gets lighter in value as you blend outward.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:27.170
Let's take some of it right down.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:29.980
Beautiful, beautiful color.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.940
and it's very transparent.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:35.360
And then yellow is a transparent yellow.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:43.960
Without washing the brush, take,

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:47.920
and go right into a small amount of alizarin crimson

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.060
without washing the brush.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.730
And we'll go right above that,

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:57.350
and let's put in a little bit of crimson,

00:01:58.040 --> 00:01:59.200
nice little pinkish color.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:10.640
the paint, blend it very well.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.440
Want it to blend together so you can't tell

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.420
where one color stops and the next one starts.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:18.570
Now we'll go into a little bit of crimson

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:20.740
and a little bit of Prussian blue.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:23.090
Very small amount of Prussian blue.

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:25.610
It's 100 times stronger than your crimson.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:27.750
And just brush mix it.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.060
Prussian blue, Alizarin crimson,

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:35.420
but a very, very small amount of blue, okay?

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:40.190
Now, here, put a little lavender color.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:45.560
This just all blends together.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:54.460
And then I'll go right into Prussian blue.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:58.790
And fill up the remainder of the sky.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.840
Now, I haven't washed the brush all the way through this,

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.770
all the way through, but you don't want to get the blue

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:07.910
and the yellow mixed together.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:10.620
If you do, you'll have a bright green sky,

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.480
and chances are you won't be happy with that.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:16.420
There we go.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.180
I've got the old dirty brush.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.740
I'm gonna go back into a little crimson and blue,

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.920
and maybe come right down here

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.500
and lay in a little lavender color.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:31.620
I'll have a little bit of water here.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:35.260
I am an absolute fanatic for water, I love it.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:39.330
It was up to me, every painting that I did

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:40.550
nearly would have water in it.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:42.430
But sometimes you have to do something

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:43.210
that doesn't have water.

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:51.540
It was over yellow, so we'll just do that for right now.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:53.010
And I'll clean the brush.

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.050
And we clean our brushes with odorless paint thinner.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.950
There's a screen in the bottom of this bucket

00:03:58.950 --> 00:03:59.970
that I scrubbed.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:00.860
Scrub the brush against,

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:03.980
shake out the excess paint thinner,

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:09.430
and then the fun, blip blip.

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:11.590
You just beat the devil out of that brush.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:12.850
Take out all your hostilities.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:14.660
Now with a clean dry brush,

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:17.060
I'm gonna blend this sky together.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:20.460
You can spend some time blending this.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:22.980
You want it to really, really blend together beautifully.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:25.360
You don't wanna be able to tell

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.760
one color stops and the next one starts.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.540
Just, just be together.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:32.740
And you can do this several times if necessary.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.200
Step back, take a look-see.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:37.790
It really pays to step away from the painting sometime

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:39.930
and look at it, get a whole different view.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:46.100
Now then, just bring this all the way across.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.380
Now that we have a clean brush,

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:49.780
we'll just bring it right across.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:58.030
Easy, we have sky and water already finished.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:07.150
Okay, now then, let's build us a little mountain up here.

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:08.110
I like mountains.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:10.590
My home's in Alaska,

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.700
and we have a lot of mountains in Alaska,

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:14.680
some of the most beautiful mountains in the world.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:18.540
So I'm gonna take Prussian blue and Alizarin crimson.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:21.530
Now you need much more crimson than blue.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:25.270
Once again, the blue is a hundred times stronger,

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:29.980
and I wanna dull that, so I'm gonna reach out.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.560
and put a small amount of Van Dyke Brown into it.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:37.830
So, crimson, Prussian blue, and Van Dyke Brown.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:41.390
I want it to have sort of a purplish cast,

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:44.470
so I'm using more crimson than I normally would.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:48.640
Now, if you want to test that, see what color it really is,

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:52.930
take a little white color and put into it.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.280
That's really the only way you can tell,

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:57.520
otherwise it just looks black in here, okay?

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.630
That gives us a pretty good color.

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:02.210
Let's take a little bit on the fan brush.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:08.100
We'll use the fan brush today to make us a mountain.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:10.760
Load that brush full of paint.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:15.010
Pull it through there, wiggle it, both sides,

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:15.850
and then sharpen it.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:18.580
Look at the amount of paint in the bristles.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:20.460
That's what we're looking for, okay?

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:21.060
Let's go up here.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:24.080
Maybe the little mountain lives right here.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.540
You have to make this decision.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:28.400
Maybe, maybe, right about there.

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:29.980
And we're using just the corner.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.320
the corner of the brush, wherever you want it to go.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:35.340
Give it some little wiggles and jiggles,

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.200
and just make all kind of beautiful little things.

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:40.260
Maybe there's a bump, wherever you want it.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:43.280
Use just the corner of the brush, that's all you need.

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:46.250
And you're not applying a great deal of paint,

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:49.160
just a little, maybe it comes down

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:53.670
and there's a bump there, wherever, wherever.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:06:59.590
Take our large brush.

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:01.290
and pull that.

00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:05.010
That removes excess paint and blends it out.

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:09.240
And if you can see the entire mountain,

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:11.480
it should be more distinct at the top

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:12.980
than it is at the bottom.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:14.860
So this happens automatically

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:16.540
because it's mixing with a color underneath

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:17.440
in the Magic White.

00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:20.490
Automatically, it gets lighter in value

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:21.930
as it goes towards the horizon.

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:23.640
See there?

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:26.900
You don't have to worry about it.

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:31.980
canvas, it'll do it for ya.

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:36.180
Got a basic mountain shape already.

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:39.570
Now then, let's take another fan brush.

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:41.230
I have several here so I don't have to spend

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:42.330
a lot of time cleaning them.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.920
Okay, load it full of titanium white.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.620
And to that, I'm gonna reach right down here

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.160
and grab a little bit of permanent red.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:55.490
Small amount, small amount, and set it on fire.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:57.050
Load a lot of paint into the bristles,

00:07:57.880 --> 00:07:59.970
a lot of paint, okay, let's go right up.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.540
Now you have to make some decisions in this mountain.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.360
Which one of these peaks is the farthest away?

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.240
You wanna do the one that's farthest away first

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:07.100
and work forward.

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:09.220
So maybe, let's start over here.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:11.720
I'm just gonna touch and wiggle it.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:12.630
Just wiggle it.

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:17.730
All these little things happen gently.

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:22.960
There it is.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:24.420
Move it around.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:25.940
Down there like that.

00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:27.810
Wherever you want it to go.

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:35.420
Oh, here we are, there it is, there, I see it.

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:38.070
Just visualize these things in your mind

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:41.140
and put them on the canvas, that's all there is.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:51.480
Now normally, normally we put highlights

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:52.560
on the mountain with a knife.

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:54.660
Today I wanted to show you that you can use

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:57.630
your little fan brush and just make all kinds

00:08:57.630 --> 00:08:58.510
of beautiful effects.

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:10.450
Just let them go, just to go.

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:12.130
Make it as wide or as small as you want it.

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:14.030
Maybe there's a little light showing right there.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:17.500
Maybe even a little back there, wherever.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:20.490
Okay, now I'll take a little Prussian blue

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:22.620
and mix right into my white.

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:25.790
Make a shadow color, we need a shadow color.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:32.960
Go back up here, once again,

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:35.710
figure out which one of these is the farthest away,

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:36.770
and do it first.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:39.240
Do the one in the back first, see?

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:41.340
Now we've done that one, now let's take a little paint,

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:43.040
come right down through here,

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:44.340
and we come directly through that.

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:46.640
Pushes that one right into the background.

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:47.780
That easy.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:49.340
Did you know you had that much power?

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:07.520
Each little highlight here needs its own private shadow.

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:11.050
So you just sort of look at what you laid in here

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:12.890
and begin working with it.

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:22.720
Here, this area.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:29.800
With all your darks, maybe there's a little shadow.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:34.700
There, it's right behind that highlight.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:38.500
Barely, barely touching the canvas.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.930
Super, super easy little way to make.

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:50.490
Very effective distant mountains.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.760
wherever you want it, wherever you want it.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:05.330
Drop it in.

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:15.520
So now, you can take these mountains

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:16.400
anywhere you want to go.

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:19.220
If you're not careful, you'll get to where you like this

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:20.820
and you'll cover up your entire canvas

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.780
with just mountains, which is wonderful.

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:24.540
It teaches you how to make mountains.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:25.740
That's the way I used to practice.

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:28.960
I would cover an entire canvas with mountains

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:29.960
and scrape it off.

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:32.400
Do it again, over and over and over.

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:35.180
And that's the way you learn, is by repetition,

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:37.890
doing things over and over, okay?

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:40.270
Now let's take a clean, dry brush,

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:42.220
and I wanna create a little mist here,

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.520
so we'll tap this, just gently, gently, gently tap.

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:47.680
Follow the angles in your mountain,

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:59.820
like there isn't some air, very, very touching, soft.

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:03.000
following those angles, most, most important.

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:06.960
Over here, tap in this direction, lift up.

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:19.020
Easy to destroy, but we just want to diffuse.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:25.820
Okay, now then, we can start playing a little bit here.

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:29.890
We'll take, this is our lavender color that we made.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.240
purplish color, same thing the mountain's made out of.

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:35.240
I'm gonna add a little bit more of the blue into it.

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.080
Give it a little more blue hue.

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:39.930
Blue hue, that's hard to say.

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:42.510
Okay, let's go back up here.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:47.080
And maybe there's a few little tree lines

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:48.360
running down the side of this mountain.

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:51.160
Touch, using just a corner of the brush, lift upward.

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:53.700
These are far, far away, we don't want detail yet.

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:02.400
You have to follow the angles that are in the mountain.

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:05.040
If you don't, it's not gonna look right.

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.520
And you're gonna be unhappy with me.

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:09.010
I want you to be happy.

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:17.200
It's all about does nice things to your heart.

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:27.280
Just make it look like the tree line

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:28.980
running up the side back here.

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:38.590
a way of creating distance in your painting.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:48.350
And I'm gonna take a clean, dry, one-inch brush,

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:52.710
and very lightly, very lightly, whisper-like,

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:56.580
begin lifting up and allowing that to mix with under color.

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:05.640
so it softens it, very soft and very distant, quiet.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.790
See, and a super way to make little distant tree lines,

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:17.920
and you don't have to do hardly a thing.

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:21.180
Just lay a little color on, lift it up,

00:14:21.530 --> 00:14:22.350
and you're in business.

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:29.120
It's not only fun, it can be easy.

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:29.960
All you need to do is...

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.950
learn a few little basic rules, and go crazy.

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:38.200
Okay, now we can get in here.

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:40.950
Let's get some more good dark color.

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:42.630
Let's just keep using the fan brush.

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:43.870
We've used it so much today.

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:46.710
Maybe, maybe, there it is.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:48.410
Make a decision, drop it in.

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:51.600
Give me a minute, drop it in.

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.160
Just sort of look at your painting

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.560
and visualize all these beautiful little things.

00:14:58.660 --> 00:14:59.420
Let them happen.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:07.630
Probably one of the hardest things is not how to paint,

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:08.840
but what to paint.

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:11.380
That's what drives most of us crazy,

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:14.850
is sitting around trying to figure out what to paint.

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:21.480
I carry a camera with me over where I go nearly,

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:24.630
and with that camera, if I see something that excites me,

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:26.350
I take a picture of it and save it,

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:29.980
because you can capture a second in time and save it.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.060
leave it till you want to use it.

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:34.780
And from that you can make beautiful paintings.

00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:38.830
And we'll give you the technique here,

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:42.250
take what you see,

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:44.260
because everybody sees nature differently.

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:47.120
You paint beautiful paintings,

00:15:48.950 --> 00:15:49.810
they'll make you happy.

00:15:51.060 --> 00:15:52.480
Okay, I'm just pulling a little bit,

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:55.670
little bit of this lavender color down.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.900
Now, if you want to make this look like it goes back here,

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:02.840
Let this reflection be shorter than over here.

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:06.960
It'll give the impression that it's round like that

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:08.080
and goes way back.

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:09.830
Sneaky, huh?

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:13.680
Okay, now very lightly come across.

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:18.120
Super light, super, super light.

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:20.570
Just enough to give it a watery appearance

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:21.610
and then leave it alone.

00:16:23.510 --> 00:16:25.430
Very, very easy to overwork it.

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:29.870
Overwork it, and we don't want to do that, okay?

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.360
Now then, let's put some highlights back in here.

00:16:32.740 --> 00:16:35.320
And I'm gonna take a little bit of permanent red,

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:42.110
red here, and we'll mix it with a little bit of yellow.

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:45.590
